{"posts":[{"id":"scotty_p6_126","t":"I did take a trade at the completion of the larger QM and then it started with its grinding compression down. However, I now see all of the 'colorful' PA after the fact\n\nFurthermore, I am thoroughly convinced that the IT's plan things very well.","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#126","p":6,"im":["dcffb8c29cccd506040ca17f7f7fd4b23b812c3a","6b88cd64f20be91c8e9d76979f826a07e63818ff"],"m":126},{"id":"scotty_p6_127","t":"Always fun when this happens. QM Love! Saw it yesterday during the NY session.","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#127","p":6,"im":["f207d52891bc3a1b0d2b392b8e8c033dd69fa8c9"],"m":127},{"id":"scotty_p6_128","t":"Well, it's about time I stop standing by and bag one of these babies!\n\nM15 EJ\n\nM1","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#128","p":6,"im":["352acacb16f211bd1d44719de114595acba04d72","7156908c6a74e8c5750d21db1b48dda6998281ad"],"m":128},{"id":"scotty_p6_129","t":"GU PA as of recent. Price is everything!","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#129","p":6,"im":["7e4a0f45fb14985ebe595a5a605c24e124c96621"],"m":129},{"id":"scotty_p6_130","t":"naascott wrote: GU PA as of recent. Price is everything!\n\nHi Scotty, manage to figure out your point here. what do you mean by 'flag becomes flag limit'?","a":"blackmovie","d":"","n":"#130","p":6,"im":[],"m":130},{"id":"scotty_p6_131","t":"Hey black, I marked the large one because it seemed to more significant - it did hold price up nicely a bit later on. A flag limit just being a pause/base before after a key level (SR, paz, etc.) with a confirming break from the pause/base with momentum (FTR) lower/higher. Hope that makes sense:)","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#131","p":6,"im":["72bc5276c57caec6ea14bc0ee55827bb725b5482"],"m":131},{"id":"scotty_p6_132","t":"Activity for today\n\nNO trade here but noticed this one 1 min. They love using the news to complete their moves.\n\nGBPCAD work Risk NO MORE than 8-12 pips (not including spread)\n\nWhat I saw playing out before taking trades above as I was looking for shorts.","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#132","p":6,"im":["523ef9bdc6f492d92c257af17c8d66196d5569f4","1e90288f06ab032a926f4f861674403b5989eda6","0972590cc33e86cf7314a4e705f0ab1fd9b0b5ce"],"m":132},{"id":"scotty_p6_133","t":"Love Spikey rises. And watching QM's unfold.\n\nBefore\n\nAfter","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#133","p":6,"im":["be8af18e3b3274f28248efefddd9ddc88265c3ab","ba8600a048982ade85016c95ee544ba45c42b2d9"],"m":133},{"id":"scotty_p6_134","t":"Having ah ha moments!","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#134","p":6,"im":[],"m":134},{"id":"scotty_p6_135","t":"Hey thanks, Alex. I almost fell out of my chair when I found that","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#135","p":6,"im":[],"m":135},{"id":"scotty_p6_136","t":"Quick Monday night Kiwi treat! Thank you New Zealand!","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#136","p":6,"im":["1b9c1826d66694fd797cb8f54855723ca74329b2"],"m":136},{"id":"scotty_p6_137","t":"took this same move","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#137","p":6,"im":[],"m":137},{"id":"scotty_p6_138","t":"Sweet Sagana! Awesome job buddy. And we made it, too","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#138","p":6,"im":["8c43017c5b85a06f58d33ebee0dc24298466e3be"],"m":138},{"id":"scotty_p6_139","t":"GBPCAD - Already bagged some profit. Looking for other side of CP.\n\nRetrace. So much interesting PA.","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#139","p":6,"im":["f3a43b11db08e558955fd3255730ea2c29484ffe","e481ba1a80bac25908fd28531b0fd90bac13b2e7"],"m":139},{"id":"scotty_p6_140","t":"Updated GBPCAD. Some great PA today. Don't really like trading news, but this was quite good.\n\nOrder flow looked good, too! I decided to re-enter here instead of my area shown above. Being that we had a small CP zone below with an engulf, I felt pretty good about it.","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#140","p":6,"im":["8162c80fd1e6ff504be4eac2b7366d99320e7cdc","1757348ee1194530cbc80601ba67f9d12261bf37"],"m":140},{"id":"scotty_p6_141","t":"can you please analyze gbpjpy, i need it please please...","a":"wom25","d":"","n":"#141","p":6,"im":[],"m":141},{"id":"scotty_p6_142","t":"Hey Wom, glad to help! But the best help I can give you is to encourage you to REALLY study the material here at RTM. This way you can have the \"ah ha!\" moments. Trust me, bud - they will come!\n\nHere's what the H4 shows us:","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#142","p":6,"im":["3a1864fce6c699afe74e02e65d7ee9dfc68e6aaa"],"m":142},{"id":"scotty_p6_143","t":"First trade for March. I got punchy, but that's okay. I have had a few days off -- it's expected.","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#143","p":6,"im":["3e67334f315d01fdbc483cee43ecfb14a98efbbb"],"m":143},{"id":"scotty_p6_144","t":"Hey Scott,\n\nRegarding the chart. My question was where can we get those editing tools such as the arrow? and the dotted lines that tell where u had entered position and exited position. Thank you Scott.","a":"lv5758","d":"","n":"#144","p":6,"im":[],"m":144},{"id":"scotty_p6_145","t":"Hey Iv,\n\nI use screen cast to upload images to. They have a free account you can use that will give you something lik2 gigs\n\nwww.screencast.com/\n\nThey have a free screen capture tool called Jing that connects to your screen cast account\n\nwww.techsmith.com/download/jing/\n\nOr you can use Snagit, which will also hook right into your screen cast account, but it's about $30, which I also have - and use mostly (How I draw my arrows, etc.)\n\nwww.techsmith.com/snagit.html\n\nLet me know if have any more questions. I am happy to help!","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#145","p":6,"im":[],"m":145},{"id":"scotty_p6_146","t":"Decided to fire up Ninja today and throw on some CL contracts. Nice and Volatile, but PA is PA!","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#146","p":6,"im":["33ae2657b6d48ef8441e37554f4adf79b5da3fbb"],"m":146},{"id":"scotty_p6_147","t":"naascott wrote: Hey IV,\n\nIn the first image of #1163. I think you may find this useful.\n\nHi Scott, I have been thinking about flip areas. I noticed there's a few flip area. But what bothers me is how do we know which ones are more important? Do we have any ways for determining whether a certain flip area is more important to the other ones? Thank you","a":"lv5758","d":"","n":"#147","p":6,"im":["d5ad8d46df6e605c2f2e0592e3b3e88be08efd59"],"m":147},{"id":"scotty_p6_148","t":"Hey IV, so it seems that HTF flip areas hold more significance than LTF areas. If I see an area where price is 'flipping'around, I always check on the HTF to see what it is, which is often quite revealing. Also, it is good to take note of what the price is around such areas. Often times, you will see round numbers. For me, I have seared the following into my brain. 00, 80, 50, 20. eg. See m15 image below and note the last two digits on the areas where you see the horizontal lines. Both are in the 80's","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#148","p":6,"im":["b33d312b485df2341e308652b5555c551ae11618"],"m":148},{"id":"scotty_p6_149","t":"A little Weekend EU Forex tester 2 Homework. A bit tedious in the 5 min base, but I thought it was neat!\n\nThis is the 5 min, zoomed view of the base in green. Impulse candles are often traps to get you to sell. Never take the bait, or you could end up being \"caged\" in and have bad things done to you","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#149","p":6,"im":["b62c764012c9fe753fc7600d933efd09d0232f43","0cedbd8db0e724d49ea3df0ccec9be9314bfcb03"],"m":149},{"id":"scotty_p6_150","t":"My advice - Scotty, mark also RBD /DBR and find key Swings and find retest of untested level.","a":"Kovalenko","d":"","n":"#150","p":6,"im":[],"m":150}],"images":[{"k":"dcffb8c29cccd506040ca17f7f7fd4b23b812c3a","t":"assets/thumbs/dcffb8c29cccd506040ca17f7f7fd4b23b812c3a.webp","f":"assets/images/dcffb8c29cccd506040ca17f7f7fd4b23b812c3a.png","w":1500,"h":666,"b":78986,"o":"dcffb8c29cccd506040ca17f7f7fd4b23b812c3a.png","p":6,"pid":"scotty_p6_126"},{"k":"6b88cd64f20be91c8e9d76979f826a07e63818ff","t":"assets/thumbs/6b88cd64f20be91c8e9d76979f826a07e63818ff.webp","f":"assets/images/6b88cd64f20be91c8e9d76979f826a07e63818ff.png","w":917,"h":474,"b":21976,"o":"6b88cd64f20